# test/parity/SECTIONS -- runtime sections that exist only when a program asks
# for them, and the program that asks.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. Parts of the Wasm runtime are emitted as literal WAT text
# rather than compiled from Mere, each gated behind a flag only a program using
# that feature sets. Text that is never emitted is never validated, never
# linked and never run -- so a representation change walks past it and nothing
# goes red. That is not hypothetical; it happened three times in one day:
#
#   Q-068  mk_logger / mk_metrics: i32 locals against i64 signatures, and a
#          Logger record with 4-byte fields where a field is 8. No
#          Wasm-compiled program in the corpus used a capability.
#   Q-069  $mere_list_len: tag read as i32 at offset 0, payload at offset 4 --
#          the layout from before values widened. Nothing called it. (LLVM's
#          list-len helper was broken twice over, separately.)
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE ENCODES: a section with no program is untested code that
# looks like tested code.
#
# MODE is which invocation reaches the section, and it is load-bearing:
#
#   plain      `mere -w`. test/parity/ compiles this way, so the section is
#              also required to be reached by SOME parity program -- the named
#              one is a pointer, not a licence.
#   component  `mere -w --component`. Three sections exist only here, and the
#              parity harness cannot reach them at all. scripts/
#              component_parity.sh builds and RUNS these against the
#              interpreter; scripts/section_coverage.sh checks the section is
#              emitted at all.
#   none       genuinely unreachable, with the reason in the last column. There
#              are none today. The status is kept because the next one should
#              be a row with a reason rather than an absence, and because
#              section_coverage FAILS if a `none` row becomes reachable instead
#              of passing quietly.
#
# section              marker                  mode       program
file_io_used           __lang_read_file_h      plain      test/parity/file_pio.mere
list_len_used          mere_list_len           plain      test/parity/list_len.mere
logger_used            __mere_logger_info_fn   plain      test/parity/logger_metrics_caps.mere
metrics_used           __mere_metrics_inc_fn   plain      test/parity/logger_metrics_caps.mere
vec_to_list_used       mere_vec_to_list        plain      test/parity/show_composite.mere
wasm_args_used         __lang_args             plain      test/parity/args_empty.mere
wasm_args_host_used    __lang_args_host        plain      test/parity/args_empty.mere
wasm_time_used         __lang_time             plain      test/parity/arith.mere
wasm_env_used          __lang_env_var          component  test/component/env_var.mere
wasm_stdin_used        __lang_read_stdin       component  test/component/read_stdin.mere
wasm_socket_ffi        sock_instnet            component  test/component/socket_ffi_shape.mere
